  "solution": {
    "text": "All these enamines are interconvertible through their resonating structures. So most stable form is &lsquo;C&rsquo; due to steric factor. All of these has the equal resonance only differ in their geometrical configuration. The enamine in option C has bulky groups on opposite side of double bond. means they have the minimum repulsion between them."
